KNOWNBUG
s_until2.sv
--bound 3
^\[main\.p0\] always \(main\.s == 1 \|-> \(main\.s == 1 s_until main\.s == 2\)\): PROVED up to bound 3$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
When encoding until/R for lasso-shaped counterexamples,
property_obligations_rec (src/trans-word-level/property.cpp) iterates
over the time frames from min(current, lasso.start), i.e., it includes
time frames before the current time frame when the loop starts earlier.
The operands are hence evaluated in time frames that precede the start
of the evaluation attempt.  With bound 3, the lasso from t=3 back to t=0
causes the attempt starting at t=1 to check the operands at t=0, and
EBMC reports REFUTED.
